        "defense": null,
        "description": {
            "value": "<p><em>Libra &mdash; 3rd (Cloth Ability) Technique, gained at level 11.</em></p><p><em>Dragon Flight &mdash; the Saint punches forward as if flying, and the dragon leaves the ground carrying the strike with it.</em></p><p><strong>Fly up to 60 feet</strong> in a straight line and make one <strong>unarmed Strike or Libra weapon Strike</strong> at any point during the movement, dealing <strong>+6d8 damage</strong> on a hit. This movement doesn't trigger reactions.</p><p>On a hit you may continue to the end of your movement; on a miss you stop adjacent to the target. On a critical hit, the target is carried with you to the end of your flight and knocked prone.</p><hr /><p><strong>Heightening (+2 levels)</strong> The additional damage increases by 1d8 and the flight by 10 feet.</p><p>On a day your constellation is <strong>Ascendant</strong> this Technique heightens as though you were 4 levels higher; on a <strong>Zenith</strong>, 8 levels higher.</p><hr /><p>Target the creature and cast: the Strike is rolled with whichever Libra weapon is in your hands &mdash; or your fist, if none is &mdash; and followed through to its damage. The flight itself is your own movement, and the range you may target is the distance you may cover.</p>"
        },
